    "text": "In `lagos-lekki-v2`, 120mm / 3h over the whole area:\n\n**Baseline** `r_19bad5451b9f8e42` vs **lagoon held 1.0 m high** `r_7d9f3940cb415e7e`\n\n> Tide here is an assumed lagoon/sea boundary level, not a forecast. Default is -0.5 m.\n\n### Flooded buildings\n\n| stat | baseline | tide lock 1.0 m | change alt-base |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| buildings_flooded | 29137 | 29567 | +430 |\n| buildings_flooded_severe | 8230 | 8585 | +355 |\n| buildings_flooded_own_cell | 12420 | 12646 | +226 |\n| people_exposed | 88124 | 90212 | +2088 |\n| road_km_impassable | 384.7 | 430.071 | +45.371 |\n| flooded_area_km2 | 21.8598 | 28.5074 | +6.6476 |\n| max_depth_m | 2.051 | 2.064 | +0.013 |\n\nMechanism in the model: `boundary_outflow_m3` goes from +1543335.4 to -4992827.9, `stored_volume_end_m3` +6491847.2 m3.\n\nInterpretation:\n* Modest rise in building count, +430 / ~1.5%, but +355 of that is severe.\n* Large rise in extent, +6.65 km2 / ~30%, with almost no rise in max depth. Tide lock spreads shallow water and prevents drainage.\n* +45.4 km more impassable road.\n\nChecked locally in `Lekki Phase 1`:\n\n* baseline: 1555 buildings_flooded, 521 own_cell, 4698 people, 18.468 km impassable, max 1.296 m\n* tide lock 1.0 m: identical - 1555, 521, 4698, 18.468 km, 1.296 m\n\nThe +430 buildings are outside Lekki Phase 1, on lower lagoon margins.\n\n### Evacuation route to nearest shelter\n\nTested from Lekki Phase 1 centre `[3.47674,6.44154]` at peak `t_s=10200` and early `t_s=3600`:\n\n* At 1h:\n  * baseline `rt_cb086abf58b1`: reachable to `Lekki British School (candidate shelter (assumed))`, 0.865 km, 13.0 min ETA, 20 edges removed\n  * tide lock `rt_62b69283a876`: reachable to same shelter, same path, 0.865 km, 13.0 min ETA, but 344 edges removed network-wide\n  * Same short route still open, redundancy much lower.\n\n* At peak 2h50m:\n  * baseline `rt_f9007e065e4d`: unreachable, 2563 edges removed\n  * tide lock `rt_27cd5946289d`: unreachable, 2886 edges removed (+323 vs baseline)\n\nSo: evacuate early. Under 1 m tide lock the local route is unchanged at 1h but the network degrades faster, and by peak no route to nearest shelter from Lekki Phase 1 in either case, with more blockages under tide lock.\n\nPlanning model, not a forecast.\n"
